+# KMS / Cosign Key Orchestration Runbook (operator)
+
+This document provides operator steps for provisioning and rotating cosign KMS URIs across environments and for coordinating audits.
+
+Steps:
+1. Provision KMS key in cloud provider (AWS KMS, GCP KMS, Azure KeyVault). Require key policy restricting usage to CI runners / cosign principals.
+2. Store COSIGN_KMS_URI in Vault and in CI secrets (org-level).
+3. Rotate key:
+   - Create new key, deploy temporary signing config to CI (COSIGN_KMS_URI -> new key).
+   - Run smoke-sign job to sign a test artifact and verify Rekor entry.
+   - Update ops/sdk/evidence_sdk.py and CI secrets to point to new key.
+   - Revoke or schedule deletion of old key after retention window.
+4. Audit:
+   - Collect Rekor entries and cosign logs; provide them to crypto auditor.
+   - Run ops/security/kms_audit_collect.sh (operator helper) and package for auditors.
+
+Notes:
+- Do not share private keys. Use KMS/HSM-backed cosign to avoid private key leakage.
+- Maintain key usage logs and alerts for anomalous signing frequency.
+
